§§ `Dieu 133: conditions for a broker's licence`

-- Dieu 133(1), (4), (5). V1: (1)(a) the right to found and manage an enterprise (Law on Enterprises); (1)(b) an organisation
-- is a lawful legal person meeting the Government's financial conditions; (4) an organisational form this Law provides and
-- a draft charter. Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 2(7) repeals (1)(a) and (4) from V2. (5): a foreign organisation holding 10% or
-- more needs 5 years of brokerage (itself or a subsidiary) and its authority's permission with 3 years free of serious breach.
@@qb 39 74
@@qa 336 337
@ref Dieu 133 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:39-74; src:law139-2025-qh15:336-337)
GIVEN f IS A `A founder of a broker`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 133(1) and (5): the founder meets the conditions` f MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the rules in force are those of V2 or later`
           THEN `the broker founder meets limb (b) and (5)` f
           IF `the rules in force are those of V1 or later`
           THEN f's `has the right to found and manage an enterprise in Vietnam under the Law on Enterprises` AND `the broker founder meets limb (b) and (5)` f
           OTHERWISE REFUSE "Law 08/2022/QH15 was not in force before 1 January 2023"

GIVEN f IS A `A founder of a broker`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the broker founder meets limb (b) and (5)` f MEANS
        (   (NOT f's `is an organisation`)
         OR f's `is an organisation with legal personality that operates lawfully and meets the financial conditions the Government sets`)
    AND (   (NOT f's `is established under foreign law and holds 10% or more of charter capital`)
         OR (    f's `has itself or through a subsidiary run insurance brokerage for the latest 5 consecutive years`
             AND f's `a foreign authority allowed it to found the broker and confirmed no serious breach in the latest 3 consecutive years`))

@@qb 50 54
@ref Dieu 133 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:50-54)
GIVEN a IS A `A broker licence application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 133(2): the capital conditions are met` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a's `minimum charter capital the Government sets`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN REFUSE "Dieu 133(2)(a) requires charter capital not below the minimum the Government sets; no minimum is supplied"
    WHEN JUST m THEN     a's `charter capital is contributed in Vietnamese dong`
                     AND a's `charter capital` AT LEAST m
                     AND (NOT a's `founders use borrowed capital or funds entrusted by others`)

@@qb 55 61
@ref Dieu 133 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:55-61)
GIVEN a IS A `A broker licence application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 133(3): the personnel condition is met` a MEANS
    a's `has a chair, a chief executive and a legal representative expected to meet Dieu 138`

GIVEN a IS A `A broker licence application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 133(4): the form of organisation and the draft charter are in order` a MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the rules in force are those of V2 or later`
           THEN REFUSE "Dieu 133(4) is repealed by Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 2(7) from 1 January 2026"
           IF `the rules in force are those of V1 or later`
           THEN a's `has an organisational form this Law provides and a draft charter consistent with the Law on Enterprises`
           OTHERWISE REFUSE "Law 08/2022/QH15 was not in force before 1 January 2023"

§§ `Dieu 134: the dossier`

-- Dieu 134. V1 lists five documents. Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 1(10) replaces the article with one sentence: the Government
-- sets the conditions, dossier, order and procedure for a broker's licence.
@@qb 77 92
@@qa 236 242
@ref Dieu 134 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:77-92; src:law139-2025-qh15:236-242)
GIVEN a IS A `A broker licence application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 134: the dossier contains the documents the Law lists` a MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the rules in force are those of V2 or later`
           THEN REFUSE "Dieu 134 as replaced by Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 1(10) leaves the conditions, dossier, order and procedure to the Government; its decree is not among the sources"
           IF `the rules in force are those of V1 or later`
           THEN     a's `has the written application`
                AND a's `has the draft charter`
                AND a's `has the 5-year operating plan`
                AND a's `has the CVs, criminal records and qualifications of the proposed officers`
                AND a's `has the capital contribution, the list of holders of 10% or more and proof they meet Dieu 133`
           OTHERWISE REFUSE "Law 08/2022/QH15 was not in force before 1 January 2023"

@@qb 91 92
@ref Dieu 134 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:91-92)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 134(2): the Government's rules on the conditions, dossier, order and procedure of licensing a broker (V1 text)` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 134(2) (V1) delegates the conditions, dossier, order and procedure to the Government; its decree is not among the sources"

`Dieu 135 — the form of organisation, foreign ownership, time to grant, authority, publication and revocation of a broker's licence follow Dieu 62, 68, 70, 71, 72 and 75(1) and (3) (a cross-reference, resolved in law08-ch3-licensing.l4 and law08-ch3-scope.l4; Dieu 71(3) is repealed from V2 but Dieu 135 cites Dieu 71 whole, so it resolves)` MEANS
    "Cross-reference to Chuong III."

§§ `Dieu 136: changes`

@@qb 101 125
@ref Dieu 136 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:101-125)
GIVEN c IS A `A change to a broker`
GIVETH A `A step the Law requires for a change`
`Dieu 136: the step the Law requires for the change to a broker` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `a change of name or of head office address`    THEN `prior written approval of the Ministry of Finance`
    WHEN `a change of charter capital`                   THEN `prior written approval of the Ministry of Finance`
    WHEN `a change of content, scope or term of activity` THEN `prior written approval of the Ministry of Finance`
    WHEN `a transfer of shares taking a holder to or above 10%, or below 10%` THEN `prior written approval of the Ministry of Finance`
    WHEN `a change of the chair or the chief executive`  THEN `prior written approval of the Ministry of Finance`
    WHEN `a division, split, merger, consolidation, dissolution, change of form, or opening a branch or other presence abroad` THEN `prior written approval of the Ministry of Finance`
    WHEN `a change of the charter`                       THEN `written notice to the Ministry of Finance within 15 days of the change`
    WHEN `opening, ending or moving a branch or representative office` THEN `written notice to the Ministry of Finance within 15 days of the change`

@@qb 116 125
@ref Dieu 136 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:116-125)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 136(4): the Government's rules on approving and recording changes of a broker` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 136(4) delegates the conditions, dossier and procedure to the Government; its decree is not among the sources"

§§ `Dieu 137: rights and duties of a broker`

@@qb 127 149
@ref Dieu 137 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:127-149)
`Dieu 137(1)-(2) — a broker's rights (commission as the Minister of Finance provides; fees for ancillary services and other work) and duties (confidentiality; compensate customers for harm; disclose what the Minister requires; account separately for sums collected or paid for insurers; buy professional liability insurance) (lists; no rule evaluated)` MEANS
    "Rights and duties."

@@qb 150 164
@ref Dieu 137 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:150-164)
GIVEN c IS A `The conduct of a broker`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 137(3): the broker's conduct is prohibited` c MEANS
        c's `prevented a policyholder from giving information or urged the policyholder not to declare it`
    OR  c's `promoted by promising unlawful benefits to urge a customer to contract`
    OR  c's `urged a policyholder to cancel a contract in force to buy a new one`
    OR  c's `advised buying from an insurer on less competitive terms to earn higher commission`
    OR  c's `gave the customer false or unsuitable information on an insurer's terms`

§§ `Dieu 138: personnel, capital, finance`

@@qb 165 182
@ref Dieu 138 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:165-182)
GIVEN f IS A `The finances of a broker`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 138(2)-(3): the broker's brokers and capital meet the Law` f MEANS
    CONSIDER f's `minimum charter capital the Government sets`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN REFUSE "Dieu 138(3) requires charter capital and owners' equity not below the minimum charter capital the Government sets; no minimum is supplied"
    WHEN JUST m THEN     f's `person who directly brokers has a degree in insurance or an insurance or broker certificate`
                     AND f's `charter capital` AT LEAST m
                     AND f's `owners' equity` AT LEAST m

-- Dieu 138(3a), added by Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 1(11): a broker's investment must be safe, liquid and efficient, lawful,
-- at its own risk, and not made in shareholders, members or their related persons (except deposits at a credit institution
-- that is a shareholder or member). V1 has no such paragraph.
@@qa 243 250
@ref Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 1 (src:law139-2025-qh15:243-250)
GIVEN f IS A `The finances of a broker`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 138(3a): the broker's investment complies` f MEANS
    IF `the rules in force are those of V2 or later`
    THEN f's `investment is safe, liquid and efficient, lawful, and at its own risk` AND (NOT f's `invested in shareholders, members or their related persons, other than deposits at a credit institution that is a shareholder or member`)
    ELSE REFUSE "Dieu 138(3a) does not exist in V1: it was added by Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 1(11) from 1 January 2026"

@@qb 165 200
@ref Dieu 138 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:165-200)
`Dieu 138(1), (4)-(8) — personnel standards by the Government; the financial year and accounting follow Dieu 103-104 with annual independent audit; reports as the Minister of Finance provides; profit transfer abroad follows Dieu 107; financial governance follows Dieu 108; disclosure on the broker's website of audited accounts and the changes needing approval and Dieu 120(1)(a), (b), (e), as Dieu 117 provides (cross-references to provisions encoded elsewhere; no new rule)` MEANS
    "Cross-references."

@@qb 203 211
@ref Dieu 139 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:203-211)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 139: the Minister of Finance's rules on broker certificates` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 139(2) delegates the training content, dossier, examination, issue, withdrawal and exchange of broker certificates to the Minister of Finance; the Minister's circular is not among the sources"

§ `Chuong IV, Muc 3: To chuc, ca nhan cung cap dich vu phu tro bao hiem`

§§ `Dieu 140 to 142: providers of ancillary services`

-- Dieu 140. Insurers and foreign non-life branches, and other legal persons, may supply ancillary services to insurers,
-- reinsurers, foreign branches, brokers and mutual organisations; brokers also to any other organisation or individual; an
-- individual may supply advice only, to those same recipients.
@@qb 219 233
@ref Dieu 140 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:219-233)
GIVEN p IS A `A provider of ancillary services`
      r IS A `A recipient of ancillary services`
      s IS A `A kind of ancillary service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 140: the provider may supply the service to the recipient` p r s MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `an insurer or a foreign non-life branch` THEN r EQUALS `an insurer, reinsurer, foreign branch, broker or mutual organisation`
    WHEN `an insurance broker` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another organisation with legal personality` THEN r EQUALS `an insurer, reinsurer, foreign branch, broker or mutual organisation`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN s EQUALS `advice` AND r EQUALS `an insurer, reinsurer, foreign branch, broker or mutual organisation`

@@qb 236 242
@ref Dieu 141 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:236-242)
`Dieu 141 — principles of supplying ancillary services: honesty, objectivity, transparency; sector standards; the code of ethics of the social-professional organisation; a written contract (principles; no rule evaluated)` MEANS
    "Four principles."

@@qb 243 258
@ref Dieu 142 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:243-258)
GIVEN p IS A `The position of an ancillary provider`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 142(2): the broker may not provide loss adjustment on the contract` p MEANS
    p's `provider is a broker that arranged the making of the contract` AND p's `provides loss adjustment on that contract`

GIVEN p IS A `The position of an ancillary provider`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 142(3): the organisation may not provide loss adjustment or claims support on the contract` p MEANS
    p's `provider is also the policyholder, insured person or beneficiary under the contract` AND p's `provides loss adjustment or claims support on that contract`

GIVEN p IS A `The position of an ancillary provider`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 142(4): the provider failed to buy professional liability insurance` p MEANS
    NOT p's `has bought professional liability insurance suited to the service`

`Dieu 142(1) — a provider keeps client secrets and uses client information only for its purpose (a duty also found in Dieu 11(3) and 129(2)(i); no separate rule evaluated)` MEANS
    "Confidentiality."

§§ `Dieu 143: conditions for supplying ancillary services`

-- Dieu 143(1)-(2). In V1 and V2 an individual giving advice needs full capacity and an insurance degree (or another degree and
-- an ancillary insurance certificate); an organisation needs legal personality, lawful operation, qualified staff, and for loss
-- adjusters and actuaries the further standards. Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 2(8) repeals Dieu 143 from 1 July 2026 (V3): V3 answers
-- that it does not exist, not with V2's conditions.
@@qb 260 282
@@qa 339 339
@ref Dieu 143 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:260-282; src:law139-2025-qh15:339)
GIVEN p IS A `A provider of ancillary services (conditions)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 143: the provider meets the conditions to supply ancillary services` p MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the rules in force are those of V3`
           THEN REFUSE "Dieu 143 is repealed by Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 2(8) from 1 July 2026; the Law then states no condition for supplying ancillary services"
           IF `the rules in force are those of V1 or later`
           THEN IF p's `is an individual giving advice`
                THEN     p's `has full civil act capacity`
                     AND (p's `has a degree in insurance` OR p's `has a degree in another field and an ancillary insurance certificate for advice`)
                ELSE     p's `is an organisation with legal personality, lawfully established and operating`
                     AND p's `its staff directly doing ancillary work have full capacity and suitable degrees or certificates`
                     AND ((NOT p's `is a loss adjustment organisation`) OR p's `its loss adjusters also meet the standards of an assessor under commercial law`)
                     AND ((NOT p's `is an actuarial organisation`) OR p's `its actuaries also meet the conditions for an actuary`)
           OTHERWISE REFUSE "Law 08/2022/QH15 was not in force before 1 January 2023"

@@qb 283 286
@ref Dieu 143 (src:law08-2022-qh15-577-578:283-286)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 143(3)-(4): the Government's and the Minister of Finance's rules on staff standards and ancillary certificates` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the rules in force are those of V3`
           THEN REFUSE "Dieu 143 is repealed from 1 July 2026"
           OTHERWISE REFUSE "Dieu 143(3) delegates staff standards to the Government and Dieu 143(4) the ancillary certificates to the Minister of Finance; neither is among the sources"
